  "question": {
    "text": "A light ray is incident perpendicular to one face of a $90^{\\circ}$ prism and is totally internally reflected at the glass-air interface. If the angle of reflection is $45^{\\circ}$, we conclude that the refractive index $n$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/667BLGA4A4cOc0N4YH8hMQduzfD6GZPmqybYNWd9hUA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PwiLY",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{n} < \\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Kr62u",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{n}>\\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Kx5xM",
      "text": "\n$n>\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Vu7XD",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{n} < \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Angle of incidence $\\mathrm{i}>\\mathrm{C}$ for total internal reflection. Here $\\mathrm{i}=45^{\\circ}$ inside the medium.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore 45^{\\circ}>\\sin ^{-1}(1 / n) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow n>\\sqrt{ } 2 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
